export const knowledgeDocuments = [{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","content":"# ProgressTracker product map\n\nProgressTracker is an offline-first personal tracker for habits, goals, challenges, and projects. The main routes are Today (`/`), Trackers (`/trackers`), Calendar (`/calendar`), History (`/history`), Analytics (`/analytics`), Goals (`/goals`), Dashboard (`/dashboard`), Holidays (`/holidays`), and Settings (`/settings`).\n\nTracker definitions and check-ins are stored locally in IndexedDB through the repository layer. A signed-in account can synchronize workspace records through Supabase. The assistant explains product behavior only; it does not read tracker definitions, check-ins, or workspace settings.\n\nSource references: `src/routes/router.tsx`, `src/app/AppShell.tsx`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts`.\n"},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","content":"# Measures and success rules\n\nEach tracker has one or more measures. New measures are Yes/no or Quantity. Existing Duration and Checklist measures remain supported. A saved measure's type and historical meaning are immutable. To track a different value, add a new measure. A measure with check-in history can be retired: it leaves future check-in forms while its definition remains available to History and Analytics.\n\nQuantity thresholds can have Minimum, Target, and Stretch levels for one check-in. They are separate from goal planning totals. Higher or lower can represent progress. Numeric values are nonnegative; an increasing success condition at zero is rejected because it would qualify every nonnegative value.\n\nSuccess rules define whether a recorded check-in qualifies. A condition can compare a value or use a configured threshold. Nested All (AND), Any (OR), and At least N rules combine conditions. Rules affect qualification and streak summaries, not the saved value itself.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/types.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/schema.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/progression.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/invariants.ts`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `supabase/migrations/20261018000100_tracker_metric_integrity.sql`.\n"},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","content":"# Schedules and streaks\n\nA schedule determines which dates are expected check-in opportunities. Standard Mode counts scheduled, non-holiday opportunities. Strict Mode counts every active calendar day, including rest days and past holidays. An unlogged current date stays open rather than counting as missed. A check-in qualifies according to the tracker success rule; streak calculations use the same qualification model and respect the active date range.\n\nChanging schedules affects future opportunity calculations, not saved check-in rows. Holidays are stored as date-only values in the workspace time zone.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/planning.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/progression.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts`, `src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx`, `src/domain/holidays.ts`.\n"},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","content":"# Goals, planning, and milestones\n\nPlanning targets are distinct from per-check-in thresholds. Daily recurring plans compare each scheduled date with a daily target. Cumulative deadline plans add eligible incremental entries toward one total and require a tracker deadline. Snapshot values are not summed. Each measure keeps its own unit and target. Allocation planning can distribute a cumulative target across scheduled dates.\n\nMilestones are checkpoints linked optionally to a measure and value. They do not create extra progress entries. The goal view compares saved progress with the checkpoint using the measure's interpretation.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/planning.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts`, `src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx`, `src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx`.\n"},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","content":"# Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync\n\nRecorded check-ins retain values by stable measure ID. History displays a measure's saved name, unit, and type, including retired measures. Analytics calculates observations for each measure separately so different units are never combined. A newer revision for a date supersedes the older revision; tombstoned entries are excluded from current check-in and trend calculations.\n\nLocal tracker edits and account sync are separate concerns. Signed-in changes enter a revisioned sync queue; the sync engine detects incompatible remote measure changes and retains a conflict for resolution. The assistant does not inspect personal records and cannot edit trackers.\n\nSource references: `src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx`, `src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts`, `src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `src/db/database.ts`.\n"}] as const
